; apps/cword/welcome.wtx - the shipped WELCOME.RTF's source (SPEC.md 73.12.3).
; Same markup and the same parser as apps/word/welcome.wtx (tools/os88doc.py
; owns parse_line; tools/os88rtf.py turns the result into RTF instead of .DOC).
;
; WHY THIS IS A SECOND SOURCE AND NOT THE SAME FILE. It was first because
; cword's RTF reader dropped every paragraph format and folded the three
; underlines into one, so the .DOC's demonstrations would have been claims the
; screen does not keep. Since SPEC.md 73.12.4 the reader and the writer carry
; every format the editor can set, and this file wears them all - so it is a
; second source now only because the two products' documents say different
; things: this one is RTF, and its key list is this port's (SPEC.md 73.12.3).
.c {d}WELCOME TO MICROSOFT WORD{/d}
.c Version 1.1a for os8088, written in C

This document is an RTF file: everything on this page - the {b}bold{/b}, the {i}italics{/i}, the centered heading above, the indents below - was saved into it and is being rendered back by the same engine you are typing into.

{b}What works{/b}
Type anywhere; select with the mouse, or press F8 and extend with the arrow keys. Character formats live on the ribbon, in Format Character, and on the Ctrl keys: {b}bold{/b} (Ctrl-B), {i}italic{/i}, {b}{i}both together{/b}{/i}, {u}underline{/u} (Ctrl-U), {w}word underline{/w} (Ctrl-W), {d}double underline{/d} (Ctrl-D) and {k}small caps{/k} (Ctrl-K). Paragraph formats come from the ruler, the Ctrl keys, or Format Paragraph.
.li 5 .fi -5 This paragraph wears a hanging indent, set with Ctrl-T; the ruler's markers show it, and dragging them moves it.
.c This paragraph is centered (Ctrl-C).
.r This one is flush right (Ctrl-R).
Line spacing, space before and justification are saved with the paragraph too; this draft view sets every paragraph single spaced and ragged right, and all of it survives a save.

{b}A few keys{/b}
Ctrl-F        Search
F4 / Shift-F4 Repeat the search down / up
F5            Go To a page
Ins           Overtype (the status bar's OVR lamp)
F8            Extend the selection (EXT)
Shift-Del     Cut
Shift-Ins     Paste
Ctrl-S        Save
Ctrl-Z        Undo
Alt-F4        Exit

View > Draft wraps the text to the window; View > Page shows the sheet it will print on. The Font list is built from the system disk's FONTS folder and sets the document in a proportional face. The menus, ribbon, ruler, status line and dialogs follow the Opus source release preserved by the Computer History Museum.
Save your own documents into the DOCS folder with Save As.
